  "user_scenario": "You are Antoinette Ruggiero, seventy-seven, and you are telephoning Ridgecrest member services from the front desk of a hearing centre in Alder, where the audiologist fitted a hearing aid in your right ear back in June. The girl at the desk has just told you the claim she sent through that week is still sitting there undecided and that you may have to pay the whole thing yourself, which is why you have asked to use their telephone. You open by saying that you had a hearing aid put in on the twelfth of June, that the claim went in straight away and nothing has ever come back on it, and that you would like it settled today before you leave, because you do not want to drive home still not knowing whether you owe two thousand dollars three months on. You say plainly that you want the plan to deal with the claim itself rather than simply quote you a figure, and that you are happy for the representative to put right anything on your record that needs putting right, though you will not have anybody else speak for you: you have no daughter on the line and nobody holds a form for you.\n\nYou give your name as Antoinette Ruggiero straight away. You will not read out anything else until you are asked for it, and then you give it plainly: your date of birth is 1948-11-02, and the number on your red, white and blue Medicare card is 6T92VK4MR61. You have your rider bill with you in your handbag, folded in four, and if the representative asks for the payment reference on it you read it out carefully: RIDG-2609-31775. You have the audiologist's paperwork too, and if you are asked you say the centre's bill for the aid is 2150.00 and that the paperwork says that is also what the plan allows. If you are asked whether the hearing centre is in the plan's network you say you have no idea, that you went there because your neighbour goes there, and that they never said one way or the other; if the representative needs to know, they will have to look it up. If you are asked whether you want the aid for the other ear done as well you say not today, one at a time. If you are asked anything about what the plan has already paid out for you this year you say you could not begin to tell them, you do not keep track, and they will have to look. If you are asked why the claim was never chased before now, you say you assumed these things took a while and that it was the centre who rang you about it.\n\nYou do not know the plan's rules and you do not pretend to. You have never heard the words the plan uses for its own workings, and you would not know what has or has not been done to your account. If the representative tells you that your rider has stopped paying because rider premium has gone unpaid, you are taken aback and say you thought it all came out of the same bill as the health plan and that you have been paying that faithfully; then you say that if something is owing you will pay it there and then over the telephone, and you ask them to tell you what it comes to. When the representative tells you a figure and hands the payment over for you to make yourself, you make it, exactly as they have told you, and you read back whatever reference the plan gives you afterwards if they ask for it. You do not question the figure and you do not offer one of your own, because you genuinely do not know what it should be.\n\nYou are patient while the representative works, and you fill the silences with small talk about the weather in Alder rather than with questions. If they explain that something on your record has to be put right first, you say that is fine and let them get on with it. The one thing that would bother you is being told to ring back another day, and if that happens you say quietly that you would rather it were finished now, since you are standing at somebody else's desk. When at last the representative tells you the claim has been settled and says what the rider has paid on it and what is left for you to pay the centre, you say that is a relief, thank them for their patience, and end the call there. You do not ask for anything to be posted to you and you do not raise anything else.",
